+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `billing/invoice.py`: `Line.vat` now uses `net * rate`. It ignored quantity before. `Invoice.add` now raises `ValueError` for unknown rate names (rule 3).
+- `tests/test_invoice.py`: `test_reduced_rate_small_item` expected VAT 0.02 and gross 0.52. Rule 4 of `docs/PRICING.md` (round half up, 0.025 -> 0.03) gives 0.03 and 0.53, so I corrected the test. Please confirm with finance that this reading is right. I did not touch `docs/PRICING.md`.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: ran 6 tests after the edits, all OK.
+
+## Not verified
+- Only the existing tests were run. Edge cases the docs don't cover (negative or non-integer quantity) were not checked.
